Vendored code: VisoMaster
-------------------------

Everything under `visoswap/` is derived from VisoMaster:

    https://github.com/visomaster/VisoMaster

VisoMaster is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 3. VisoSwap
vendors VisoMaster's inference code, so that license attaches to this project as
a whole -- GPLv3 here is forced, not chosen.

Every vendored file carries a four-line attribution header naming VisoMaster as
its origin. `tests/test_vendor_headers.py` fails the build if any vendored file
loses it.


Provenance of the vendored copy
-------------------------------

Vendored from : D:/Visomaster  (local working copy)
Source path   : D:/Visomaster/app/processors/
Vendored on   : 2026-08-21

Upstream revision: COULD NOT BE DETERMINED.

The source tree's git metadata is unreadable. Every `git -C D:/Visomaster ...`
invocation fails with:

    fatal: bad config line 1 in file .git/config

This is a pre-existing condition of that working copy, not something VisoSwap
caused; the tree is treated as read-only source material and was deliberately
not repaired. No commit SHA could therefore be recorded.

This is stated explicitly rather than left blank. An unrecorded provenance is
what makes a later GPL audit expensive; an explicitly-unknown one at least tells
an auditor exactly where to look and why the answer is missing. Anyone needing
the exact upstream revision should diff `visoswap/` against a freshly cloned
VisoMaster checkout -- vendoring is a byte copy plus a mechanical import rewrite,
so such a diff stays meaningful.


Model weights: insightface -- NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY
-----------------------------------------------------

This is a separate obligation from the GPL and is not covered by it.

The insightface model weights this project depends on are licensed for
non-commercial research purposes only. That includes `genderage.onnx`, which
VisoSwap's face selection relies on to identify a confident female face before
falling back to the most prominent one.

VisoSwap may therefore not be used commercially while it depends on those
weights. This restriction blocks nothing about running, modifying, or
redistributing the source under the GPL; it blocks any commercial deployment.

    https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface


